  "id": "COMPOUND:9138 - PROTEIN:1381",
  "verbalization": "Calcium gluconate is implicated in the interaction with Beclin-1 through multiple indirect pathways, all of which converge on the 72 kDa type IV collagenase and other related molecules. The evidence suggests that Calcium gluconate acts as a target for several compounds, including N-[(3-hydroxy-4-methoxyphenyl)methyl]-7-methyloctanamide and Spongia-13(16),14-Dien-19-Oic Acid, which in turn target Beclin-1. This indicates a potential regulatory role for Calcium gluconate in modulating the activity of these downstream molecules, which may ultimately influence Beclin-1 function. The presence of multiple pathways involving different targets highlights a complex network of interactions, where Calcium gluconate may exert its effects through a series of molecular intermediates. The integration of these pathways suggests that Calcium gluconate could be involved in a broader regulatory mechanism that affects Beclin-1, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
